User:
Please solve this issue: # Issue #3938: [BUG] SSE transport connection passes an
invalid argument to MCP's client class

### Description

When initializing an MCP client while creating a connection to an MCP server 
using SSE transport, an invalid argument (`terminate_on_close`) is passed. The 
argument is valid for [streamable HTTP 
transport](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/blob/main/src/mcp/
client/streamable_http.py#L452C5-L452C23), but is not supported for [SSE 
transport](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/blob/main/src/mcp/
client/sse.py#L25-L32). This results in a crash when trying to run an agent that
connects to an MCP server using SSE transport.

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Start an MCP server using the 
[server.py](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23605043/server.py) script
2. Run the 
[agent.py](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23605064/agent.py) script 
where an agent tries to use the MCP server

### Expected behavior

The agent successfully establishes a connection to the MCP server

### Screenshots/Code snippets

N/A

### Operating System

macOS Sonoma

### Python Version

3.12

### crewAI Version

1.5.0

### crewAI Tools Version

N/A

### Virtual Environment

Venv

